{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/extension.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.729846Z","id":"e63a6a28fafb18a57f9f09db75ebb6066e303494f17c2e62fab3f0b9ffff7d51","body":{"detail":"Admitting /api/questions and /api/inbox for the extension credential with Rule::Any widens the extension's live-only posture (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-05-chrome-overlay-design.md section 9.5). docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:902-915 lists what it lets the extension see and states this is an open owner question. Decision needed: keep this, or restore the live-only posture by filtering /api/inbox and /api/questions to live-page items for the extension, leaving out other items' artifact, and refusing the item and question routes for items that are not live.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":219},"end":{"line":225},"content_hash":"42fd645df0331ac3b918c79febc1ed9c76e9816106613f5ffb3ce2598683cf75"},"summary":"The extension, acting as the owner, may list and read every inbox item and question, gallery artifacts' included","tags":["status:needs-decision","security","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.729928Z","id":"08c71b1d8fdc76e191c83edb2af71e563c9e741bfd851209a15560352f303926","body":{"detail":"holds_owner_topics() is true while any owner stream holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs:159-161 uses it to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":922},"end":{"line":934},"content_hash":"f6adc3ed660939059f9e64510a13e36ab574c2ccd5ad2970222e0018fb7ae42a"},"summary":"A hidden owner tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730370Z","id":"0bcf4f587cf928d2e3c178b4c665dd3ef96b626dc96bcdc039c83c93d78d459f","body":{"detail":"A LAN viewer (the clax_viewer cookie) can create viewers, threads, comments, sends and db documents without limit. Decision needed: add rate limits for LAN writes, and at what rates.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":28},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"9a53d622c5cd382d1f2001c30cabb62990539edb252653358aeb36f3bb3ab7e4"},"summary":"LAN viewers' writes have no rate limit","tags":["status:needs-decision","security","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:38:28.460204Z","id":"094670e659f246fd8c0fb11fb220081c0e63397c77dc17e42625146fa39f9c08","body":{"detail":"holds_owner_topics() is true while any owner stream holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs:159-161 uses it to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":928},"end":{"line":940},"content_hash":"f6adc3ed660939059f9e64510a13e36ab574c2ccd5ad2970222e0018fb7ae42a"},"summary":"A hidden owner tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"08c71b1d8fdc76e191c83edb2af71e563c9e741bfd851209a15560352f303926","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:18:44.696797Z","id":"299c217d4da8b89af20a6fab35682f3421f0f61db5ee1cd6886ee5dd8979910a","body":{"detail":"Decided merge order: toolpath-audit lands on main first, and the multi-person branch adapts at its rebase (the plan is recorded in that branch's ledger). What this code does to multi-person's callers today: a request authenticated by a Clax-Grant token (Caller::PersonAgent, Caller::Person in crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs on that branch) has Identity.token false, so audit_actor here falls through to ensure_viewer and records Actor::Anonymous (no cookie), and git_field/call_field in crates/clax-server/src/audit.rs ignore its x-clax-git and x-clax-call because they count only with the daemon token. Multi-person makes the CLI run under a harness Caller::OwnerAgent (X-Clax-Channel: agent); this branch records it as the owner on via cli. Both branches take migration 23.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":252},"end":{"line":283},"content_hash":"936968f2ff2b30bed6a10c0e73a306cf1efd6f75699ee922e3687cf6d8bb8892"},"suggested_fix":"At multi-person's rebase onto main: derive the audit actor from Caller (add person and person-agent actors, with the grant ID, to spec 2026-10-06-toolpath-audit-design §5.2 and §10.1); accept the agent-side headers from any verified agent channel; settle one channel header (x-clax-via or X-Clax-Channel); add kinds for invite and grant approve, deny and revoke, or list those routes in the route guard's UNAUDITED with a reason; renumber multi-person's migrations after AUDIT_MIGRATION (23) in crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs, in the same commit as the migration array; and backfill nothing for people and grants, since they arrive after the audit migration and record live.","summary":"When multi-person merges after this branch, it must make the audit actor name its callers: as it stands a grant-authenticated agent is recorded as anonymous, with its git and call headers dropped","tags":["review","merge","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/audit.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:18:44.697257Z","id":"8332fed85a14d8fe76860cec95e283dfa09fdb53abb32b66b5e6e1f8a96dd88c","body":{"detail":"The extractor's own job costs one interactive round trip before the handler's. Measured with a scratch test against TestServer (debug build, 4 runtime workers, 300-400 sequential requests, three rounds): GET /api/_test/audit/ctx, which is only the extraction, p50 201-227 us against /healthz 144-157 us at idle (about 60 us per job); with 8 clients looping on GET /api/viewers/me, a one-job route at p50 411-420 us, p95 557-566 us, and the extraction alone p50 426-445 us, p95 572-1316 us, so each audited write pays about one more queue wait. Agent tool calls also add one writer transaction for tool.call and, under Claude Code, one for tool.call_id, read-only tools and each wait_for_feedback included. The perf gates passed on unchanged budgets (docs/verification.md §10). Not fixed in the branch's final round: 23 handlers in seven route modules (artifacts, assets, docs, feedback, live, sites, threads, plus the live refile context) take AuditCtx, each with its own job structure, so moving the resolve into their jobs is a change to every audited route rather than a cheap one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":282},"end":{"line":291},"content_hash":"fde9f6c59006fc734d792edc237fec3e153f53108171e787e2ff1539a90cf319"},"suggested_fix":"Take DeferredAudit in the handlers and resolve it inside the handler's own store job, as the session routes already do with for_session.","summary":"Every request that records an event now takes two interactive store jobs: the AuditCtx extractor resolves the actor in its own store_call before the handler's","tags":["review","perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:49:28.381696Z","id":"638aaaa49bf1032d1120dbf2fa174bee536bde9e2584b1f21ee9fa0a39623487","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() releases a hook question to the terminal at once when it is about no artifact: none named, no live working record, and Store::session_artifact (crates/clax-core/src/store/watches.rs) finds no live artifact the session watches (publishing watches). So a session that has published or watched nothing asks in the terminal whatever Clax tabs are open. A session with a page still waits in Clax while a hidden owner tab holds the questions topic (holds_owner_topics, unchanged), so the question in this thread is still open. Tests: crates/clax-server/tests/api_questions.rs a_hook_question_waits_in_clax_only_once_its_session_has_a_page, a_hook_question_waits_beside_a_page_its_session_watches.","kind":"comment","references":"094670e659f246fd8c0fb11fb220081c0e63397c77dc17e42625146fa39f9c08","summary":"Narrowed, not settled: a mirrored question now waits in Clax only once its session has a page","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:27:15.661323Z","id":"046a9a2ea7406525331ed75a3a1f88150fa27fd11ac1b3f96959cc985b603432","body":{"detail":"Every handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":761},"end":{"line":761},"content_hash":"95e634966fc956bcf03f44fdf7131faa6bc9307f6e163a961719bf6f762fe602"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve Person/Viewer lazily in Agent<N> (only a person's agent needs the store), or fold the read into the handler's own store_call.","summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.969905Z","id":"53497777fd813ab94fbd75e380defdcd9678638d6182373cf2ab599e53e42dc7","body":{"detail":"Every handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":768},"end":{"line":768},"content_hash":"95e634966fc956bcf03f44fdf7131faa6bc9307f6e163a961719bf6f762fe602"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve Person/Viewer lazily in Agent<N> (only a person's agent needs the store), or fold the read into the handler's own store_call.","summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"046a9a2ea7406525331ed75a3a1f88150fa27fd11ac1b3f96959cc985b603432","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.619234Z","id":"a54a3063b96fef31c587959ab0751c1138df8e6cd506a8e53fd98b05edca9e52","body":{"detail":"holds_owner_topics() is true while any owner stream holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs:159-161 uses it to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":943},"end":{"line":955},"content_hash":"f6adc3ed660939059f9e64510a13e36ab574c2ccd5ad2970222e0018fb7ae42a"},"summary":"A hidden owner tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"094670e659f246fd8c0fb11fb220081c0e63397c77dc17e42625146fa39f9c08","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/audit.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.619361Z","id":"f2075a1688947b87c9c407943835d210a623aae8186e884a9276f6af3d98cf04","body":{"detail":"The extractor's own job costs one interactive round trip before the handler's. Measured with a scratch test against TestServer (debug build, 4 runtime workers, 300-400 sequential requests, three rounds): GET /api/_test/audit/ctx, which is only the extraction, p50 201-227 us against /healthz 144-157 us at idle (about 60 us per job); with 8 clients looping on GET /api/viewers/me, a one-job route at p50 411-420 us, p95 557-566 us, and the extraction alone p50 426-445 us, p95 572-1316 us, so each audited write pays about one more queue wait. Agent tool calls also add one writer transaction for tool.call and, under Claude Code, one for tool.call_id, read-only tools and each wait_for_feedback included. The perf gates passed on unchanged budgets (docs/verification.md §10). Not fixed in the branch's final round: 23 handlers in seven route modules (artifacts, assets, docs, feedback, live, sites, threads, plus the live refile context) take AuditCtx, each with its own job structure, so moving the resolve into their jobs is a change to every audited route rather than a cheap one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":324},"end":{"line":333},"content_hash":"fde9f6c59006fc734d792edc237fec3e153f53108171e787e2ff1539a90cf319"},"suggested_fix":"Take DeferredAudit in the handlers and resolve it inside the handler's own store job, as the session routes already do with for_session.","summary":"Every request that records an event now takes two interactive store jobs: the AuditCtx extractor resolves the actor in its own store_call before the handler's","supersedes":"8332fed85a14d8fe76860cec95e283dfa09fdb53abb32b66b5e6e1f8a96dd88c","tags":["review","perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:29.091800Z","id":"8853a213149854df4a55296ccdb35b78ad6ecec83873bf99b2f30909149e124a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:56a4b01","summary":"Fixed: the audit actor comes from the verified credential as Caller counts it (Identity::audit_actor): a grant's agent is recorded with grant_id and person, sessionless or not; the token with X-Clax-Channel: agent (the CLI under a harness, the hooks, Pi) is an agent naming its channel; a connected person's browser is a viewer marked person. x-clax-via, x-clax-git and x-clax-call count on every verified agent channel, grants included. Audit spec §5.2, §6.8, §6.13 and §10.1 and multi-person spec §20 amended. invite.*, grant.*, person.rights, person.revoke and agent.name are recorded; the grant, invite and agent-rename routes left UNAUDITED. Multi-person's migrations are 24-26 (PEOPLE_MIGRATION = 24, in 98390dd). People and grants arrive after the audit migration and record live, so nothing is backfilled. /api/admin/perf/calibrate takes DeniedToGrants. Evidence: cargo nextest run --workspace at 56a4b01, 1864 passed, including api_toolpath::a_persons_agent_is_recorded_with_its_grant_and_person, api_toolpath::the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent, api_toolpath::a_connected_persons_browser_is_a_person, api_toolpath::a_terminal_answer_reported_by_a_persons_hook_is_the_persons, store::people::tests::the_grant_flow_records_who_did_what_without_secrets, api_grants::the_grant_routes_record_their_events, toolpath::tests::every_recorded_kind_is_classified_and_renders_conformant, routes::l10::every_change_route_resolves_the_audit_context_or_says_why_not and api_agent_auth::a_grant_credential_is_refused_wherever_no_need_is_declared. Commits 9440f16, ea4daf0, 56a4b01.","supersedes":"299c217d4da8b89af20a6fab35682f3421f0f61db5ee1cd6886ee5dd8979910a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T14:21:06.258764Z","id":"aad27e37c6fc12484dd639d56fdd0b30bd06e13e6870f9d185cc2bd8f085b86f","body":{"detail":"Identity::caller makes the token an OwnerAgent whenever a session is named (path or X-Clax-Session), known or not; audit_actor records an agent only for a known session of the token's, the agent marker, or x-clax-via mcp, else the owner. Measured through GET /api/_test/audit/ctx: Authorization Bearer + X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 (no session) and X-Clax-Session not-a-ulid both give {\"type\":\"owner\"}. Today's clients send the marker, so this bites only an older or third-party agent side; it breaks audit spec section 5.2's rule that one request is never an agent to Caller and the owner to the journal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":463},"end":{"line":470},"content_hash":"75fc91286c48244768b0a0e9a1d2af39937a039081897bf71644933e706cbb12"},"suggested_fix":"When the token names any session that is not known, record the sessionless agent (channel as named, else mcp) instead of the owner; add the case to the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent.","summary":"The token naming an unknown or non-ULID session without the agent marker is recorded as the owner, while Caller counts it as OwnerAgent","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:36:09.887173Z","id":"7d89e4e77522e8ff2359c3da115a8dd41a10ea26c8a53a4599223fae6627ec6c","body":{"detail":"Every handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":794},"end":{"line":794},"content_hash":"95e634966fc956bcf03f44fdf7131faa6bc9307f6e163a961719bf6f762fe602"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve Person/Viewer lazily in Agent<N> (only a person's agent needs the store), or fold the read into the handler's own store_call.","summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"53497777fd813ab94fbd75e380defdcd9678638d6182373cf2ab599e53e42dc7","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:36:09.889592Z","id":"ed5c69bb5870602cc3b34334d49b4add684d766f08c59adc9ed954a488d8c2f7","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":743},"end":{"line":787},"content_hash":"ddf90a27cffb9eae9f415b9f193ba4f15b3c221446be555e0e4c03e03e2abb50"},"suggested_fix":"Settle the meaning in spec §8.3; count withheld fields instead if the shell or tools need it.","summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:36:09.889633Z","id":"87daec884cc95683a485ff5a143d5137b038df13fa968d9c7bdceb27abb1fc7f","body":{"detail":"Withhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":693},"end":{"line":720},"content_hash":"05c56d201c29c0092d6039e9c09166c4bdf07ea63e935e45f87326bf15b12593"},"suggested_fix":"Read the reader's open and declined requests for the artifact once per listing and look each thread up in memory.","summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/viewer.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:36:09.889674Z","id":"96c44912cb51710b6ff473b0919ef2b0efb660968cef25be8fd6150360a95ee0","body":{"detail":"A Clax-Grant caller writing a thread or a comment without author_kind agent is attributed to its grant's person (author_public_id, display name), as the token's agents are to the owner. Storing it as an agent comment with its session would show it as the agent's in the shell, but a thread's first comment is a viewer comment (NewThread) and a viewer comment forwards the thread, so the semantics would change. Authorship, which the filter needs, is right either way.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":106},"end":{"line":121},"content_hash":"83ee2c4a800f2125d8a2bab39db59a095b257bef4fe8d7cf0c04be3b50037d7d"},"summary":"A person's agent's viewer-kind comment is stored as its person's viewer comment, not as an agent comment","tags":["revisit:when the shell shows which agent wrote a person's comment","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/db_caller.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T22:14:39.268542Z","id":"28e2f708c283ec49b60a239dc76fbe14af843559bec3d366a5c29114f13f111f","body":{"detail":"CallerParts answers x-clax-via: page on a Clax-Grant request 400 invalid_via_page, so no document write of a person's agent is credited to a page's authors. While the docs needs are outside agent::FILTERED_LIVE, Agent<Docs*> answers 503 not_yet first, so no test reaches the refusal. When the docs routes open, each write route (PUT, PATCH, DELETE …/docs/{*path}, docs:batch, docs:str_replace, docs:acquire) needs a test that Sam's agent, from its session, sending x-clax-via: page gets 400 invalid_via_page and writes nothing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":170},"end":{"line":173},"content_hash":"ab4ff55db55f94fa691454298679f1270828dc9b9e9e97c7e0a5d4bac16987d7"},"summary":"The docs routes' refusal of the page marker from a grant is untested until they open to a person's agent","tags":["people","depends:task-11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T22:15:09.538083Z","id":"c5fb6cb91520b29b37d5bb583759013b3c084414bbf2311b02cb53f359960cb6","body":{"detail":"Every handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":886},"end":{"line":886},"content_hash":"95e634966fc956bcf03f44fdf7131faa6bc9307f6e163a961719bf6f762fe602"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve Person/Viewer lazily in Agent<N> (only a person's agent needs the store), or fold the read into the handler's own store_call.","summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"7d89e4e77522e8ff2359c3da115a8dd41a10ea26c8a53a4599223fae6627ec6c","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T22:15:09.538415Z","id":"7698f84f4ddfd1f495a7e8a0a557892dce5b4346622bdc7d3fb070b5a841bf1c","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1016},"end":{"line":1060},"content_hash":"ddf90a27cffb9eae9f415b9f193ba4f15b3c221446be555e0e4c03e03e2abb50"},"suggested_fix":"Settle the meaning in spec §8.3; count withheld fields instead if the shell or tools need it.","summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"ed5c69bb5870602cc3b34334d49b4add684d766f08c59adc9ed954a488d8c2f7","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T22:15:09.538662Z","id":"702536cf20e66da98e8a21de7e93155947593984f5e750400cb80681ac2f2448","body":{"detail":"Withhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":966},"end":{"line":993},"content_hash":"05c56d201c29c0092d6039e9c09166c4bdf07ea63e935e45f87326bf15b12593"},"suggested_fix":"Read the reader's open and declined requests for the artifact once per listing and look each thread up in memory.","summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","supersedes":"87daec884cc95683a485ff5a143d5137b038df13fa968d9c7bdceb27abb1fc7f","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
